    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation for `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the original owner is returned with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\n**Changes** \u2014 three tiny new units plus two small YAML edits, keeping structural impact low (no existing method was grown, and every touched/new function has near-zero surrounding complexity):\n\n- `IdempotencyStore.java` (new) \u2014 a `@Component` singleton mapping key \u2192 owner id (`ConcurrentHashMap`, `putIfAbsent`).\n- `CheckIdempotency.java` (new) \u2014 new **first step**. Reads `@RequestHeader(name=\"Idempotency-Key\", required=false)`. On a store hit it loads the original owner and responds 200; otherwise it calls the `@Flow(\"proceed\")` branch to run the normal pipeline.\n- `RecordIdempotency.java` (new) \u2014 runs right after `SaveOwner`; records `key \u2192 owner.getId()` when a key was supplied.\n- `owners.POST.yml` (edited) \u2014 added the `check` entry step with `outputs: { proceed: validate }`, and inserted the `record` step between `save` and `logAudit`.\n\n**Design notes**\n- No existing function was modified \u2014 all create-path logic (validation, quotas, audit, 201 response) is untouched, so non-idempotent POSTs behave exactly as before (`key == null` \u2192 straight to `proceed`).\n- The header is read independently in both new steps via `@RequestHeader`, avoiding any shared-variable plumbing (and it never touches the single-read `@RequestBody`).\n- `required=false` yields `null` when the header is absent, which both steps guard on.\n\nFull test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS** (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
