    "probe_text": "The YAML confirms the exact ordering. Here is what actually happens, in order, when a request hits `POST /api/owners` (full runtime path `/petclinic/api/owners`, since `server.servlet.context-path=/petclinic/`).\n\nThe endpoint runs through the OfficeFloor pipeline in `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 the starter dependency **is** present in `pom.xml`, so the YAML is live, and there is no leftover Spring `@RestController` for owner creation. Every step runs under one transaction that commits at the end.\n\n## Ordered list\n\n**0. Authorization** (`composition.authorize`) \u2014 `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. But `petclinic.security.enable=false` in the default profile, so this is effectively off.\n\n**1. CheckIdempotency** \u2014 reads header `Idempotency-Key`. If already seen (in-memory `IdempotencyStore`), **short-circuits**: loads the original owner and responds **200**, skipping everything below. Otherwise proceeds.\n\n**2. ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 binds body as `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (\u26a0\ufe0f **no `@Valid`**, so the DTO's JSR-380 constraints never run). Manually requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, (`addressLine1` OR `address`), `city`, `telephone` \u2192 else **400**.\n\n**3. ValidatePostcode** \u2014 if `postcode` present: must match `[0-9]{4}` and fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) \u2192 else **400**.\n\n**4. NormalizeTelephone** *(mutates)* \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164 (`+61` assumed, drops leading `0`); validates length \u2192 else **400**.\n\n**5. NormalizeEmail** *(mutates)* \u2014 if email present: must match an email regex \u2192 else **400**; lower-cases it.\n\n**6. RejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 if email present, domain must not be in blocklist (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else **400**.\n\n**7. NormalizeAddress** *(mutates)* \u2014 trims/collapses/upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET etc., composes from address lines; blank result \u2192 **400**.\n\n**8. EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 scans all owners; same telephone **and** email \u2192 **409**.\n\n**9. EnsureUniqueHousehold** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`: `householdId` = SHA-256(lastName|postcode); collision with an existing owner \u2192 **409**.\n\n**10. EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 \u2265 50 existing owners in the same city \u2192 **409**.\n\n**11. BuildOwner** *(side-effect: creates entity)* \u2014 maps DTO\u2192`Owner`; rejects a future `registrationDate` (**400**); defaults null to today and rolls off weekends/2026 holidays to a business day.\n\n**12. EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 \u2265 100 existing owners on that (rolled) registration date \u2192 **429**.\n\n**13. AssignCustomerCode** *(mutates)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n\n**14. DeduplicateCustomerCode** *(mutates)* \u2014 appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until the code is unique.\n\n**15. AssignNamesakeCount** *(mutates)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` from existing same-name owners.\n\n**16. SaveOwner** *(side-effect: persist)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; this is where the **entity's** own Hibernate constraints (`@NotEmpty`, E.164 `@Pattern`) actually fire, surfacing as `DataIntegrityViolationException` if violated.\n\n**17. RecordIdempotency** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` for future replays.\n\n**18. LogAuditOnCreate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line.\n\n**19. RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 builds `OwnerDto` (deriving displayName, membershipNumber, locality, points/level, duplicate hints, etc.) and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **The DTO's declared bean-validation is dead.** `ValidateOwnerFields` binds the body without `@Valid`, so the `@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Email`/`@Size` constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` are never enforced at request time. The only field checks that run are the hand-written ones in the function classes above, plus the entity-level constraints at `SaveOwner`.\n- The `Location` header is hardcoded `/api/owners/{id}` \u2014 it omits the `/petclinic/` context-path that the rest of the endpoint lives under."
